# Use the image CMD/ENTRYPOINT instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile ENTRYPOINT is a boot wrapper that runs the WordPress entrypoint
# (deploying the vulnerable really-simple-ssl 9.0.0 plugin into /var/www/html)
# and apache in the BACKGROUND, then execs `sleep infinity`. So:
#   * apache is ALREADY serving when the agent starts, so the verifier can prove
#     the vulnerable plugin is live-deployed by fetching it over HTTP;
#   * PID 1 stays `sleep infinity`.
#
# WordPress re-reads plugin files on every request, so removing/upgrading the
# plugin takes effect immediately — there is no "not restarted" case here.
